First let's start with the new information:

Crafty Survivors Soundtrack will be available soon!
It will be released on Steam after we finish setting everything up and we will make an announcement for it later.

Patch Notes - v1.0.4

Adjustments
Hanvilton, the Blacksmith

Adjusted the invincibility frames from the Talent In the Zone, as players could get hit instantly after finishing a Forge/Repair if surrounded by enemies. Now it has a short window after finishing the Special Command animation.


Fixes

Fixed an issue when certain characters die during special animations, where they wouldn't revive properly;
Fixed a navigation bug with the controller when choosing the Colosseum to play and going back to the area selection screen;
Fixed a bug and the behaviour with Sewvia's Talent Sewing Sisters. 1 Stack of Dodge should not spawn anything and Max Stacks (6) was bugged;
Fixed a bug with Hanvilton effects from the Talents In the Zone and Blacksmith's Grit, as they were persisting if a player dodged to cancel the Forge/Repair Command;
Fixed an issue with Theodore's Level Up UI, as the hotkeys to select the 3rd and 4th skill were not working properly.

Patch Notes - v1.0.3

Fixes

Fixed a bug with Conductor Elixir and its skills when playing with Stoverick;
Fixed a bug with Conductor Elixir's skill Arid Melody, as it was not working properly;
Fixed an issue with the Starfishes as they were not being defeated properly, remaining in the field and dealing damage;
Fixed some typos on skills;
Fixed a bug with Jewellia's achievement, as it was not triggering for some people.

If you don't get the achievement automatically, try entering an Area, the Character Selection Screen and exiting back to the Area Selection.

Patch Notes - v1.0.1

Fixes

Fixed the navigation with Gamepad for the Kitchen and Laboratory as it wasn't working as intended;
Fixed the description of Secret #58;
Fixed the description for Wallie's Clothing Skill Percussive Maintenance at Level 1 as it was showing the wrong skill;
Fixed an issue where all Great Maligmic type bosses were not giving the proper Quality for Newston's photos;
Fixed a bug with Newston's Privileged Information Skill, as it was freezing the game when Newston levelled up;
Fixed the New Achievement "Bustling With Life", as it was checking the wrong number of characters.

Patch Notes - v0.10.0.1

Adjustments

Keyra's Master Talent - Chain Reaction:

Limited the amount of Special Keys that can be spawned from the reaction of this Talent, to reduce performance issues from too many keys.

Changed confirmation Button for picking up a skill from Left Shift to Space Bar, to avoid issues with Steam Overlay.


Fixes

Fixed the missing information and ingredients from Grand Hydra's elixir;
Added a few fail safes for some Boss and Challenge achievements, as some players were not granted the achievement when conditions were met;
Fixed the display of the Accessibility Dodge Icon for the Locksmith, as it was showing a number when she doesn't have stacks;
Fixed Gamepad navigation in the Village between the new building and other existing buildings.

Hello Crafters,

We are back from our small break to continue the development of Crafty Survivors.

We are going to start with a few necessary fixes from the latest update here:

Patch Notes - v0.9.0.1

Adjustments

Various elixir skill’s effects were not being affected by the Opacity setting.


Fixes

Fixed an issue with Theodore’s Hearts Healed and Self Inflicted hits stats not showing properly at the end of the stage;
Fixed a bug with Jewellia’s weapon attacks (Loupe) were not triggering food effects that depend on an amount of attacks to trigger their effects;
Fixed Monet’s completion jewels as they were not showing on the character selection screen. This was just a visual bug, the completion status was being properly saved;
Fixed a visual issue with the Desert Area as 2 stages were labeled as Stage 3B. This is now fixed;
Fixed an issue with special unique items from certain stages as they could be picked during the level up screen with 0 amount. This would cause some problems on the game’s progression if the player chose the item. Now it will show another option for collecting extra golds instead in these situations;
Fixed a bug with some of Jewellia’s skills as they had no Limit Break options, which lead to the level up screen freezing and possibly crashing the game.

Patch Notes - v0.8.0.1

Fixes

Fixed 2 Secrets from the Mailbox as their info was wrong;
Fixed the Cavern Map Boss Stage as it was showing the wrong material;
Fixed a bug that would break the playable character when facing dual bosses.

Patch Notes - v0.7.0.4

Fixes

Alchemist’s Combination guide position adjusted as Boss Health Bars were in front of it.


Fixes

Fixed an issue with Trick or Treat System as it was not saving properly between game sessions;
Fixed an issue that made it impossible to skip unlocked characters on gamepad while selecting character presets on the Restaurant and Laboratory;
Fixed an issue with Inner Battery Passive as it would sometimes trigger multiple times while playing with Mausolea;
Fixed a bug where players were not sent to the proper area after leaving the colosseum screen, making it possible to enter areas not yet discovered;
Fixed an issue with Viala's Noxious Miasma that could cause the skill effect to not disappear after the duration was over;
Fixed a bug that would give players certain Achievements on Easy difficulty when it was not supposed to.

Patch Notes - v0.7.0.3

Fixes

Fixed an issue with Mausolea, the Gravekeeper, that could cause the game to freeze and become unresponsive to player input. This seemed to be fix on all our testing so far, but please, notify us on the Bug Reporting Subforum if this issue still happens for you;
Fixed an issue with Agriana, the Farmer, where Removing 4 skills and rerolling would break the 4th slot forever, and further removes could break even more slots. It is now possible to remove the skills without breaking the slots. Players are now able to make a Cropless run with Agriana (for whatever reason);
Fixed an issue on the Colosseum that would give players the achievement for completing areas without even playing those areas;
Fixed a bug with Mausolea that would grant multiple critical chance buffs on the UI from collecting back the Head;
Fixed a bug with Axel, the Lumberjack, where a combo between Chopping Whirlwind and Cumulus Thunder would create a cumulative permanent buff of Movement Speed that got out of hand;
Fixed an issue with 2 of Mausolea's skills, Lone Wolf and Nocturnal Acquaintance, as they were sharing information they were not supposed to and bugging each other in-game.

Patch Notes - v0.6.2.6

This small update is adding a few things and getting the game ready for the debut of Mausolea in the near feature.

Adjustments

Added a new Letter when completing Cavern Stage 8, as part of the lore to follow up in future updates. Just enter the Cave Area once and the Letter will be delivered if you have already completed Cavern Stage 8;
Added new Letters to the system to be ready for the next update. Those will only be unlockable in the next update, but they are already part of the System. (The Letter above is the last, so there will be a temporary gap in numbers);
Added new Letter Backgrounds for some characters.


Adjustments

The Farmer’s crops will not be affected by opacity settings anymore.


Bug Fixes

Adjusted some of the Lumberjack’s skills that used lumber as they had their cooldowns work in strange ways on the first use;
Fixed an issue with the explosions caused by the Curse debuff as they weren’t dealing damage;
Letter Number 12 was added again to Forest Stage EX 1 as it's asset was missing.

Patch Notes - v0.6.2.3

Adjustments

Corrupted Mage:

Reduced the range to trigger her Teleport Skill;
Reduced the range she would keep from the player when attacking, in order to improve her behaviour close to the edge of the Stage;
The Corrupted Mage doesn't collide with the boundaries of the arena, so teleporting outside of the arena should not be an issue anymore, as she will come closer to the player now before teleporting again.

Make It Rain:

The Statue will stop working when the last enemy/boss is defeated on a Stage and stop dropping gold;
The Statue won't work on Explorer Mode anymore, as it is not supposed to be active when there are no enemies left.

Bundled several Art Assets to improve performance and reduce game size.

Bug Fixes

Fixed an issue with the Sculptor's Bravery Idol as it was not applying its buff to the other Statues in its area of effect;
Fixed the amount of Speed the Great Maligmics can acquire by pulling gold in and being able to teleport through the battlefield. The amount of speed increase has a limit now;
Fixed an issue in the Forest Area, where the Stage S2 would be complete automatically if players left the area and came back before completing the Stage;
Fixed an issue where enemies could die by debuffs if the player was defeated, causing the game to break. When the player is defeated, enemies won't take damage anymore.

Patch Notes - v0.5.0.3

Adjustments

Adjusted navigation for Beach Stage 7 using the controller


Bug Fixes

Fixed a bug with the Croaking Peak's mud rings as they were not dealing damage as they were supposed to. The attack is supposed to be hazard;
Fixed an issue with Agriana's Chilling Mist and Soothing Sage not working properly with certain Foods, causing the character to be stuck;
Fixed the pre-requisites for Viala's Weaving System skill "Emergency Vial" as it was available without getting the pre-requisite skill. Please, refund skill points to avoid any future issues;
Fixed a bug with Stages that would grant recipes/designs as rewards as they would show these as collectables on a level up after reaching the maximum level;
Fixed an issue where closing a Tutorial panel during a level up would soft lock the game;
Fixed an issue that prevented players to choose extra materials on a level up screen when max level of skills was reached;
Fixed an issue that prevented the controller from opening the Level List of buildings in the Village;
Fixed a visual issue with Stoverick's and Viala's Mail Backgrounds, as they had a mockup Village behind;
Fixed an issue with the Mail System as it would not open properly if a player closed it on a page different from the first one, regardless of the section;
Fixed an issue with the title of the Forest Swamp tutorial inside of the Help Section.

Patch Notes - v0.5.0.2

Adjustments

Reduced the spawn time of the Frogolems on the Living Peak Stage.


Bug Fixes

Fixed an issue with the Alchemist's skill tree where it was grabbing information from the Blacksmith's tree for both the Weaving and Smithing Systems. Please, reset the skill points for Viala to make sure they are working properly;
Fixed an issue with the Alchemist's skill tree on the Smithing System, where certain skills could be activated without their pre-requisites;
Fixed an issue with Deity's Resemblance Marble Level Up descriptions, as they were showing their wood descriptions instead;
Fixed an issue with Deity's Resemblance Marble version not working properly;
Fixed the Completion Jewel display for Viala, the Alchemist, as it wasn't showing when completing stages in any difficulty level;
Fixed an issue with Botanic Marvel as it was not combining with other skills as intended;
Fixed a typo on the Azure Scare Menace name;
Added a failsafe to teleport the Corrupted Archer back to the battlefield if it leaves the boundaries of the Stage. We are still working on improving his collisions with the Stage to avoid this, but for now this will help players that run into this issue so they won't be stuck in the and have to fail the Stage on purpose;
Fixed the display of the Buildings Levels showing greyed text at a few levels under certain circumstances.

Patch Notes - v0.4.1.2

Bug Fixes

Fixed the missing crop (Mint) on the Farming System to upgrade the Farm;
Fixed the missing images of the new Statues unlocked on the Sculptor's Gallery;
Fixed an issue with Hanvilton's Claymore not triggering food effects like the Starlight Delight;
Fixed an issue with Hanvilton's Motivational Boost (upgrade chance buff) not applying correctly;
Fixed a collision with the new Field Event Water Cougar (Aquougar), as it was pushing players away;
Other bug fixes.

Patch Notes - v0.4.0.6

Adjustments

Change the materials dropped by Forest Stage EX1 and Forest Stage EX2. They will now drop all of the area’s materials;
Increased the size for the hitbox of Stoverick’s Knife, Axel's Axe, Hanvilton’s Dual Axes and Claymore,  so they hit enemies if they are really close to the player;
Adjusted the SFX of Stoverick's Knife, as it was using the wrong sound;
Other audio changes and adjustments.


Bug Fixes

Fixed an issue with enemies not resetting their stats properly after death. No more Bears with zoomies!
On some instances the Mountain Area would not unlock when defeating the Forest’s Boss. Added a check to help players in this situation unlock the area. Unfortunately the boss will need to be defeated again;
Fixed an issue with the Forest Swamp Tutorial not being saved as seen so it wasn’t showing up on the tutorials screen and was repeating every time players entered Forest Stage 5;
For players who utilized the Restoration Branch to get their progress back some tutorials weren’t appearing again. They should show up properly now.

Patch Notes - v0.4.0.2

Bug Fixes

Fixed an issue with Cozy Campfire's indicator not working properly;
Fixed the colour of the Chopping Whirlwind attack not matching the Axe's charge level;
Fixed an issue with the collision of trees on the Secret Paths of the Grasslands and the Forest.

Patch Notes - v0.4.0.1

We are fixing issues created with the collisions of the game created while we were trying to make some improvements to performance. Some interactions between colliders were missing due to these latest changes and a few instances were missing.
Make sure to update the game to this version to fix these latest issues.

Bug Fixes

Fixed an issue where characters could not save Axel, the Lumberjack, at the end of the Stage;
Fixed an issue with Collector's Idol and its collision as it was not collecting anything;
Fixed an issue with Heroic Technic using the Axe, as the skill was not firing the projectiles as it was supposed to;
Adjusted the navigation of the Mountain Stage 2A on the area selection screen.

Patch Notes - v0.2.2

New Features
Accessibility

Added a setting to adjust the opacity of Player Skills;
Added a setting to adjust the opacity of Player Objects, such as statues, crops, ovens, etc;
Added a setting to adjust the opacity of Particles;
Added a setting to display a small Dodge Icon UI close to the Player character.

Cast Settings
Manual and Auto cast settings will now be saved per character, so you can have different settings depending on the playstyle prefer on each of the characters in the roster.

Adjustments
Agriana, the Farmer

Fully Grown Crops won't have their indicator anymore, to reduce excess information on screen;
Adjusted the Farming radius to collect Crops, to avoid having to retreat and go back to the Crop;
Corntling Gun Buffs and Changes:
Lvl 2 - Added an increase firing rate of 30%;
Lvl 4 - Added an increase in damage of 50% per shot;
Lvl 5 - Removed the effect that doubled the amount of ammo. Added an increase firing rate of 30% and an increase in movement speed while firing by 20%.

Broccammer Buffs and Changes:
Lvl 2 - Increased the size of the attack by 50%;
Lvl 4 - Increased the size of the attack by 50%;
Lvl 5 - Removed the effect that doubled the amount of uses for the weapon. Added an effect that causes 2 extra impacts around you in the 4 diagonal directions every time the Broccammer is smashed on the ground.

Carrodrill Buffs and Changes:
Lvl 2 - Added an increase on critical hit chance of 15%;
Lvl 3 - Added an increase on critical hit chance of 15%;
Lvl 5 - Removed the effect that doubled the amount of uses for the weapon. Added an effect that fires a Drill in the direction you dash, dealing damage to all enemies in its path.

Chilling Mint Nerf:
Increased the cooldown of the Skill required to plant a Mint Seed;
Increased the interval between attacks dealt by the Chilling Mint.

Earthy Thyme Nerf and Fix:
Decreased the size of the Earth Spikes on higher levels;
Fixed the Earth Spike circles on higher levels, that were spawning the wrong combination.

Soothing Sage Nerf:
Increased the cooldown of the Skill required to plant a Sage Seed;
Decreased the size of Soothing Sage attacks on all levels.

Axel, the Lumberjack

Axel can now use Lumber Skills and Hatchet’s skills while charging his own skills;
Auto charged skills will not cancel skills that are being charged manually anymore;
Axel can now move while charging his skills. Movement speed will be reduced by 60% when charging a skill. Skills will charge faster when the character is NOT moving;
Chopping Whirlwind will now display the correct colour for the Attack Swipe.


Bug Fixes

Fixed the layering issue with Agriana's Till Soil skill, where the Soil would have priority over attack indicators. Attack Indicators will have priority over the Soil now;
Fixed an issue with the Merchant’s UI when navigation through empty slots;
Fixed the material for the Forge that was requesting 710 of the wrong material.

We want to thank everyone that's been supporting us and playing the game so far, sharing their feedback, words of encouragement and everything! Thank you!

We are currently working on the next playable character and new systems to be added to the meta-progression of the game on a bigger upcoming update, so stay tuned!

Patch Notes - Version 0.1.3.3

Settings

Save Data can now be deleted from the Settings Menu from the Title Screen. Saves cannot be deleted when going to the Settings Menu from inside a Stage. THIS ACTION IS PERMANENT, so be careful when clearing the data.


Adjustments
Axel, the Lumberjack

Reduced the cooldown of Stump Smash to 7 seconds;
Reduced the cooldown of Lumbering Hurl to 7 seconds;
Reduced the cooldown of Stake Lance to 3 seconds;
Reduced the cooldown of Dowsing Log to 3 seconds;
Reduced the cooldown of Nature's Power to 3 seconds.

Stoverick, the Chef

Changed Chef’s Knife description on Lv 5 to avoid confusion, as it could mean Stoverick would do 4 slashes when in reality he does 3.


General

Changed the visual of the chest dropped by bosses at the end of the stage and its UI when collected;
Changed the Reroll Skills input on the gamepad from R2 to L1 to reduce situations where the player would do an undesired reroll;
Optimized collision handling to improve performance.


Bug Fixes

Fixed the description of Chef’s Knife lvl 6 as it would not show up properly on the pause menu tooltip;
Fixed an issue where Axel and Sewvia would slide forever if hit while charging a skill. They are now immune to knockbacks while doing these actions;
Fixed an issue that made it impossible to cancel Sewvia’s skill Custom Fitting by dashing;
Fixed an issue that was granting Sewvia an extra dash charged on the beginning of the run;
Fixed an issue with Sewvia's yarn balls Basic Attacks, where they would keep below the flying enemies, without hitting them.



About the optimization applied to this patch:

Before this patch, skill colliders, enemy detectors and enemy attacks would check collisions with each other. That could really sink the performance when a lot of enemies were on the screen or when using a skill that creates multiple objects.

Caramel Drop Lvl 5 was a very good example for this behavior. When all extra puddles showed up the performance could take a hit and combined with another skill on top of it could make things even worse. Now they don’t care about each other so this doesn’t happen anymore.

The same would happen with tons of enemies that shoot projectiles as their detectors would check against each other.

We hope that these chances make the game more enjoyable for everyone!

Patch Notes - Version 0.1.3.2

Bug Fixes
General

Reverted the visual layer of the Mushrooms in the Forest, to have proper visibility over scenario assets;
Fixed a bug where enemies would respawn with previously afflicted debuffs (like bleeding);
Fixed an issue with the boss stage spawning more monsters than required;
Added missing icons for Numpad Numbers when rebinding keyboard controls;
Other bug fixes.

Patch Notes - Version 0.1.2

Characters
Axel, the Lumberjack

Chopping Whirlwind adjustment:

Lv 3 does not increase duration anymore, instead it will increase the speed of the rotation. The duration was so big that you could use it almost all the time.
All Lumber skills were too overpowered, as hoarding Lumber would allow for an insane burst on bosses without any delay between attacks. So all Lumber skills are being nerfed:

Added a 5 seconds cooldown to Stake Lance, Dowsing Log and Nature’s Power.


Village

Reduced requirements to upgrade Restaurant to level 1;
Reduced requirements to upgrade the earlier levels of the Forge.


General

Magnetic Force Passive buff:

Increased the power of Magnetic Force on all levels.
Chests obtained through mini bosses now give materials in case all current obtained skills are already on their max level. This fixes a bug where a skill given would have the "Roasting Time" description and crash the game.


New Settings

Added a Gamepad Left Stick Deadzone Setting. This will help avoid unintended movement from controller drifts;
Added a Graphic Setting with Display Mode to change from Fullscreen to Resizable Window;
Added a Accessibility Setting, with a Character Outline option that adds a Dark Outline on main characters that have visual priority.

More options in the Graphic Settings and Accessibility Settings will be added through future updates.

Bug Fixes
Characters

Fixed the cooldown of Cozy Campfire, as it was set to 0. Cooldown has been properly adjusted to the value it should be;
Fixed a bug where the skill Dynamic Duo would stay in cooldown forever if Water Slide was set to auto and used as soon as Hatchet joined Axel;
Fixed a bug with the pre-requisites for Axel’s premium materials where the skill never appeared on level ups;

General

Fixed a problem with the Forge Building, as it was giving the wrong upgrades after lvl 4. It is now properly increasing Weapon Damage on all available levels;
Fixed a problem with the Tailor Shop, as it was giving the wrong amount of Dash Cooldown in a few levels;
Some UI actions could be triggered by some keyboard keys. These are now removed to avoid accidents;
Fixed a bug where in some situations an already completed stage reverted back to its not completed state (red stage);
Fixed a bug where stages with multiple entrances were not showed properly;
Adjusted character movement for gamepads to try avoiding unintentional movements. Please let us know if this helps those who had problems with the gamepad, as this issue doesn't happen with any of our controllers, so we don't have means to test it.

Patch Notes

General Gameplay

Tooltips, auto setup and swapping skills are available in the level up UI;
Added a menu option to change the direction of dodge between movement and target.


Bug Fixes

Fixed a bug where pulling skills such as Flambé and Moon's Allure would work on the Great Maligtopus. They don't pull the boss anymore;
Fixed a bug where the Tentacles of the Great Maligtopus were being pulled by pulling skills such as Flambé and Moon's Allure;
Fixed a bug with rebinding movement controls on keyboard;
Fixed Sewing Journey, where Sewvia would get stuck on trees or area boundaries;
Fixed Font settings to show some characters properly, such as the É on Flambé;
Other bug fixes.
